# How much of the system each filing's stack holds, and what decided it. One row per filing: the
# typed extent, and the basis prose that is required beside it.
#
# Why it exists
#   The emitter once asserted the answer: every document carried the sentence *a partition of
#   layers claimed exhaustive*, hardcoded, where almost no filing claims `complete`. That is not a
#   `loses`: the artifact said something the other filings decline to say, which is the `invents`
#   state in the emitter's own prose. No law here reaches a string literal in a `writeln!`,
#   because it is not a count of anything.
#
# Three states, and BPMN renders one
#   `complete` asserts a boundary, `scoped` says somebody established what lies outside and
#   excluded it, `unbounded` says nobody looked. `tLaneSet` has no extent attribute of any kind,
#   and the schema's own gloss is the accusation already written: *a model that renders them
#   identically cannot tell a bounded selection from an unexamined one*. Run
#   reports/scope_declared.sqlc for the split across the corpus.
#
# The basis travels; the observation does not
#   The basis travels and the coupling observation does not, and that was measured rather than
#   assumed. `diagrams/dependences.sqlc` refuses its prose because some observations carry a numeral
#   onto a page with no unit. No basis carries one, so the same refusal does not apply here, and
#   applying it anyway would be a rule remembered rather than run.
#
# BPMN is finer on the basis
#   BPMN is the finer of the two on the basis and has nothing on the extent. `tLane` carries
#   `partitionElement` and `partitionElementRef` for what a partition is by, per lane, where this
#   model files one basis per stack. That is the grain axis running backwards for once.
#
# Defined, not read
#   A program reads these columns, so this statement defines its vocabulary in its own
#   WITH clause: a view keeps the rows and loses the column's origin, which is where
#   NOT NULL lives. assets/sqlc/views.sqlc says what a definition is.
#
-- pm:Stack/pm:StatedScope; carried as the laneSet's own documentation beside the coupling search.
WITH
scopes AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(epistemics/scopes.sqlc)
)
SELECT s.filing, s.extent, s.basis
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/scopes.sqlc)
) s
